A||||5||Max The Chainsaw||Set to "Heat", blows out of "Defroster"||||1||
Z||000000||Max The Chainsaw||10-26-2001||03:09 AM||||Hi, I got a weird problem with both my Fiero's. When I set the controls to "Heat", the air blows out of my defroster ducts. All the other buttons blow out like they are supposd to. <P>Do I have a bad door motor? Anyone know which one? <P>Thanks for any help, my feet starting to get cold.....   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||falconhulk||10-26-2001||08:00 AM||||I thought the same thing with mine. When switching from defrost to heat you hear the motor turn and if you put your hind in front of the duct it actually opens and blows for a second then closes.  Very strange.  On air cond it opens and blows fine.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Joe Torma||10-26-2001||11:47 AM||||Mine does that once a year.  Kind of a pain to fix...there is a motor with a peg that spins around an opens the 2 doors appropirately inside.  Its behind the radio, but taking it out isn't useful.  The E-clip pops of then the one arm pops off.  <P>You'll have to take off the plastic duct on the right side(like your going to replace the heater core) and get your arm in there.  <P>Feel around, the E-clip doesn't go to far.  Push the vent, heater, ac buttons until you can pop the arm on(you may have to stop it mid-motion--tun off the key).<P>Then put the clip on.  If you can't find the clip...I used a master link clip from a bicycle chain.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Max The Chainsaw||10-26-2001||11:59 AM||||Thanks. I'm gonna have to try that. Kinda thought it might be a common occurance sine both my Fiers did it.<P>Thanks again!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||10-26-2001||03:37 PM||||The all outlets will always blow some air. The doors are intentionally made so they don't seal tight inside the duct.<P>What you are describing does sound like a mode problem tho. It's posible a linkage came off. It's worth checking.<P>99% of mode door issues will be with the motor behind the radio. The other one only moves when the AC is set into or out of max cool. That's the only time the recirc door is moved.<P>While it's apart, put a little brake grease on the pin with that the linkages attach to. Brake grease won't run or stink like some others.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Max The Chainsaw||10-27-2001||07:38 AM||||Thanks Ogre. I sure appreciate it. Maybe I can keep my feet warm this winter after all.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Thanks to you all.<BR>||||reg||1
